WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.089
Think of a door frame pushed sideways. Top and bottom are parallel, and so are the sides. That shape is a parallelogram: both pairs of opposite sides are parallel and equal. Vectors can prove it.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:28.124
Parallel vectors point the same way, or opposite ways. One is a number times the other. Six i plus nine j is three times two i plus three j, so they are parallel.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:38.747
If one pair of opposite sides are equal vectors, the shape is a parallelogram. A trapezium has just one pair of parallel sides, so also show the other pair is not parallel.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:47.881
This type asks you to prove a shape, or show three points are collinear, which means on one straight line. Give the vectors, the multiple, and a conclusion.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:02.133
Step one: decide which vectors to compare: opposite sides for a shape, or two vectors from a common point for collinear points. Step two: find each, end minus start.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:13.643
Step three: show one vector is a number times the other. A parallelogram needs equal vectors. A trapezium needs the other pair shown not parallel.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:22.778
Step five: write a conclusion sentence. The trap is writing they are parallel with no working, or forgetting the final sentence.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:41.472
January twenty twenty. Vector A B is seven i plus p j, A C is eleven i minus p j, and A D is four i minus two p j. Show that, for all p, A B C D is a parallelogram. Three marks.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:50.451
We compare opposite sides. A D is given. We need B C, so we can compare A D with B C.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:02:00.985
Vector B C is end minus start: A C minus A B. Eleven i minus p j, minus, seven i plus p j, gives four i minus two p j.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:10.860
Compare. Vector A D is four i minus two p j. That is exactly vector B C. So B C equals A D.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:21.076
Equal vectors have the same direction and length. So A D and B C are parallel and equal. This holds whatever p is, because p appears in both.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:32.537
A tempting wrong route is to test one value, like p equals one. That only proves the shape for p equals one. The question says all values of p.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:44.896
So B C equals A D: opposite sides are parallel and equal. So A B C D is a parallelogram for all p. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:55.191
A common mistake is writing that two sides are parallel, with no working. The marks are for the vectors, the multiple, and the conclusion.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:16.551
Now you try, from November twenty twenty five. A B is two a plus four b. A C is seven a plus seven b. A D is ten a plus six b. Show that A B C D is a trapezium. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:30.382
Vector B C is A C minus A B: five a plus three b. Vector A D is ten a plus six b, which is two times B C. So A D is parallel to B C.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:44.241
Vector D C is A C minus A D: minus three a plus b. A multiple of A B would need k equal to minus three halves, and one quarter. Impossible, so they are not parallel.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:55.952
So exactly one pair is parallel, and A B C D is a trapezium. The most common wrong answer stops after A D equals two B C. The second pair must be tested too.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:01.393
Remember: choose the pairs, find the vectors, show the multiple, and write the conclusion.
